00:01:06.753 --> 00:01:09.017
- So a lot of the most successful
businesses that were ever

00:01:09.017 --> 00:01:11.059
founded were by people
that were scratching their

00:01:11.059 --> 00:01:12.259
own itch.

00:01:12.259 --> 00:01:13.513
You see a problem,

00:01:13.513 --> 00:01:16.252
you see something out
there that you don't like,

00:01:16.252 --> 00:01:17.329
you want to solve it,

00:01:17.329 --> 00:01:18.726
and so you go out and do it.

00:01:18.726 --> 00:01:20.520
This is what makes
entrepreneurs successful.

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:22.754
This is what separates
us from everyone else.

00:01:22.754 --> 00:01:24.503
Most people see a problem
and what do they do?

00:01:24.503 --> 00:01:26.202
They complain.

00:01:26.202 --> 00:01:28.266
Most people just complain.

00:01:28.266 --> 00:01:29.745
They complain about the government,

00:01:29.745 --> 00:01:31.743
they complain about the
transportation system

00:01:31.743 --> 00:01:33.663
and they complain about all
the negative things that are

00:01:33.663 --> 00:01:35.283
happening in their life.

00:01:35.283 --> 00:01:38.495
And they advocate
responsibility by complaining.

00:01:38.495 --> 00:01:39.993
Where entrepreneurs,

00:01:39.993 --> 00:01:42.255
we're the ones who do something about it.

00:01:42.255 --> 00:01:44.390
We're the ones who see
that negative and we turn

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:46.752
it into an opportunity for ourselves.

00:01:46.752 --> 00:01:48.380
And so if you see yourself complaining,

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:51.009
see yourself wishing that
something else had been created

00:01:51.009 --> 00:01:52.507
to solve this problem,

00:01:52.507 --> 00:01:54.487
go out and solve the problem.

00:01:54.487 --> 00:01:56.731
And then you can sell the
solution to other people.

00:01:56.731 --> 00:01:58.236
So when I look at my
first software company,

00:01:58.236 --> 00:01:59.660
it was a BioTech software company.

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:02.001
It was stared by two researchers who

00:02:02.001 --> 00:02:03.598
were at a university,

00:02:03.598 --> 00:02:05.887
and they wanted software

00:02:05.887 --> 00:02:09.276
that could help them do their
experiments more simply.

00:02:09.276 --> 00:02:11.115
To reduce the number of steps,

00:02:11.115 --> 00:02:12.697
to improve the efficiency

00:02:12.697 --> 00:02:15.008
and to create a more
visual product that people

00:02:15.008 --> 00:02:16.287
could understand.

00:02:16.287 --> 00:02:17.120
And nothing existed.

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:19.213
Everything was super
scientific and super technical,

00:02:19.213 --> 00:02:20.531
and they didn't understand how to use it.

00:02:20.531 --> 00:02:23.015
And so they built a better
version for themselves,

00:02:23.015 --> 00:02:24.273
and they shared it.

00:02:24.273 --> 00:02:26.938
And that was the genesis
of the first product.

00:02:26.938 --> 00:02:28.529
If I look at this YouTube channel,

00:02:28.529 --> 00:02:31.023
a lot of the videos that we end up doing

00:02:31.023 --> 00:02:32.225
are requests.

00:02:32.225 --> 00:02:34.256
